# 🐛 bug report

If an imported symbol is conditionally referenced, a declaration is created in that scope, and it may not be initialized for following references.

## 🎛 Configuration (.babelrc, package.json, cli command)

package.json:
```
{
  "devDependencies": {
    "@babel/core": "^7.0.0",
    "react": "^16.13.0",
    "react-dom": "^16.13.0"
  }
}
```

`parcel build index.js`

## 🤔 Expected Behavior

No error occurs.

## 😯 Current Behavior

```
/path/to/app/dist/index.js:8549
$dab9de5d978d909db2660c4851$$interop$default.render($ea7b41558fa2f98$$interop$default.createElement("div", null), document.getElementById('app'));
                                                                                      ^

TypeError: Cannot read property 'createElement' of undefined
    at /path/to/app/dist/index.js:8549:87
    at Object.<anonymous> (/path/to/app/dist/index.js:8550:3)
```

## 💻 Code Sample

index.js:

```js
import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom';

if (false) {
  console.log(React)
}

ReactDOM.render(
  <div/>,
  document.getElementById('app'),
)
```

The compiled output looks like this:

```js
if (false) {
  var $ea7b41558fa2f98$$interop$default = $parcel$interopDefault($ea7b41558fa2f98$exports);
  {
    console.log($ea7b41558fa2f98$$interop$default);
  }
}

var $dab9de5d978d909db2660c4851$$interop$default = $parcel$interopDefault($dab9de5d978d909db2660c4851$exports);
$dab9de5d978d909db2660c4851$$interop$default.render($ea7b41558fa2f98$$interop$default.createElement("div", null), document.getElementById('app'));
```

## 🌍 Your Environment

| Software         | Version(s) |
| ---------------- | ---------- |
| Parcel           | parcel v2 @ f2a62434adbba86bdd56774833d70d7852988ed1 and mischnic/dev @ 6135d13acc63260e4bd4cb3175b6fc38ad79daaa
| Node             | v12.16.1
| npm/Yarn         | yarn 1.21.1
| Operating System | macOS 10.15.3

